To create a web page about the latest news in technology, you can use HTML and CSS. Here's a simple example to get you started:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Latest Technology News</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
        }
        header {
            background: #333;
            color: white;
            padding-top: 30px;
            padding-bottom: 30px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .container {
            width: 80%;
            margin: auto;
            overflow: hidden;
        }
        .news-item {
            border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 20px 0;
        }
        .news-item:last-child {
            border-bottom: none;
        }
        .news-item h2 {
            color: #1a1a1a;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Latest Technology News</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="news-item">
            <h2>New AI Innovations in Healthcare</h2>
            <p>Recent developments in artificial intelligence are transforming healthcare by improving diagnostics, drug discovery, and patient care.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="news-item">
            <h2>Apple Launches New MacBook Pro</h2>
            <p>Apple has just unveiled its new MacBook Pro, featuring a powerful M1X chip and an updated display technology.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Add more news items as needed -->
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

This basic HTML structure includes a header and several news items with titles and brief descriptions. You can expand on this by adding more news items, styling the page further, and integrating with a real news API to fetch the latest technology news automatically.

